Notebook[{
Cell["IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"9ce582ff-7305-8c49-a632-77479c496ac5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"IsomorphicHypergraphQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"hg1", ",", " ", "hg2"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"deabf535-1b9b-cd4e-9384-761c0ee71f40"],
 " ",
 "gives True if hg1 and hg2 are isomorphic as labelled hypergraphs."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"de69d7c3-a361-5a49-a705-14604f39c6d0"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"57f664b7-823e-7e4f-adeb-b49f4fc74d38"],

Cell["\<\
Some renaming of vertex identifiers must carry hg1 onto hg2: the edge \
multisets must match exactly, each edge matching up to its own symmetry type, \
with edge multiplicities preserved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6884812f-cc25-4f46-b7ea-3ced84685ac0"],

Cell["\<\
The renaming must also carry the labels of hg1 onto those of hg2 by a \
one-to-one correspondence. Labels are therefore significant only up to \
renaming: what must agree is which elements share a label, not what the \
labels are called.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"878c126a-dc3c-9c41-a792-a9e96839803c"],

Cell["\<\
Vertex labels and edge labels are put in correspondence independently of one \
another.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d8f8a625-cf82-dc47-beb4-3d839e148817"],

Cell["\<\
An element with no label can correspond only to an element with no label. \
Without this, every unlabelled hypergraph would be isomorphic to a labelled \
one whose labels were all alike.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e48838a5-9a7d-944c-8892-6dd6ea231862"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"15dbeb83-4fd5-bb49-809c-7d7594f01f09"],
 " the skeletons are compared instead, ignoring labels altogether. Labelled \
isomorphism always implies isomorphism of skeletons."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"86d4b06d-1215-c847-bb85-bc99f31b59af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Method", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f7eb252-af3f-4546-8f10-c8af3795bf88"],
 " option is as for CanonicalHypergraph. Both settings always agree here."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b95736c7-5638-8f46-8407-050e98a4e2a9"],

Cell["\<\
The search is exhaustive, and is comfortable up to roughly eight vertices.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"55ee8e19-13b8-bc46-8999-76414e997589"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"d40d93d2-9d85-3840-93f7-5cc2d3ef7ccd"],

Cell["The same directed path on different identifiers:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"3ab61839-3591-254e-bbbe-c905c620a5ec"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{10, 20}, \
{20, 30}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}], Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {1, \
3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"06c89dff-56b5-b841-9f9c-ee2a30a24ca4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "False"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"5c4709c9-\
b296-9f4f-bbdb-eb0bc11ac3c0"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types are respected: a directed path is not an unordered one, but an \
unordered path on three vertices is an unordered star:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"87edbaf6-5c04-9549-9135-830ff9e214a3"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}],
                       Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Unordered\"], Edge[{1, 3}, \
\"Unordered\"]}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"08cc4a0f-22e1-8d42-ad62-ea35c152a52b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"e8bbd843-\
cd30-9e45-951c-4a8e5d6df9d4"],

Cell["\<\
Labels count only up to a one-to-one renaming. Here a, b corresponds to x, y:\
\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"8070d9bd-3741-214c-a4bc-70a244f15f9e"],

Cell["\<\
h1 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"a\"], Edge[{2, 3}, \
\"Directed\", \"b\"]}];
h2 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"y\"]}];
IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7747d138-c514-0749-81f9-5f1e0b10b728"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"ad782967-7403-ac48-aa12-0f8f5feaac7a"],

Cell["\<\
But h3 repeats a single label where h1 has two distinct ones, and no \
correspondence can do that:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"fc7ef1bd-018a-1544-86b1-7c660329ac49"],

Cell["\<\
h3 = Hypergraph[{Edge[{4, 5}, \"Directed\", \"x\"], Edge[{5, 6}, \
\"Directed\", \"x\"]}];
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3], IsomorphicHypergraphQ[h1, h3, \"Labeled\" -> \
False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9cd2dc1e-6ac0-7844-a781-b84153c8e18e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"5e7316f0-\
e757-3842-b1d7-5437f1492637"],

Cell["\<\
The same principle governs vertex labels. A, A, B against A, B, B is not an \
isomorphism, because A would have to correspond to both A and B:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ff2fb699-42c7-5644-8e73-80226b310e32"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"A\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"B\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"A\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"C\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}],
   Hypergraph[{Vertex[1, \"C\"], Vertex[2, \"B\"], Vertex[3, \"A\"]}, {{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"016b1dc5-d61e-354f-a64b-0783295dc11d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"53c14d04-\
3129-2f43-b5a7-bebf94ac97d5"],

Cell["An unlabelled edge is not a labelled one:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f2ae2a8a-e206-3e48-8bab-f393936b6758"],

Cell["\<\
{IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}]],
 IsomorphicHypergraphQ[Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}, \"Directed\", \"f\"]}], \
Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}]}],
                       \"Labeled\" -> False]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"87b194da-9fc4-2244-b104-85b8c1bb5fcb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"False", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"9186efc3-\
37a1-8e47-9716-c897ddce3877"],

Cell["Source", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"e299e6a2-b856-8748-8727-f9a2d7a26b25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Defined in ",
 StyleBox["src/Hypergraph.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontWeight->"Plain"],
 ", section ",
 "\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 "Canonical form and isomorphism",
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b96d2375-177f-1044-a51c-5dd777654b35"],

Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection",ExpressionUUID->"d7347cbe-79f5-4147-a027-9dfafb786937"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindHypergraphIsomorphism", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"dc2062dd-80e0-664c-8592-d6684f958235"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"db67bccd-9c13-ef42-85f8-86abe96f7dc4"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphSkeleton", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"36dcc9d3-b5af-6a41-b12c-143ad2576b9b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1c5c1c45-8684-8f4b-8745-fb3c1d21f7ba"]
}], "SeeAlso",ExpressionUUID->"4ae7b579-58c0-3a4f-9c31-2e31cff3f5f8"]
},
WindowSize->{800, 750},
